% Binding Tariff Information of EU customs offices (EBTI,
% https://ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/dds2/ebti/) run through the SAME
% plastics model (plastics.le, with gri.le) as the US rulings.
%
% One scenario per ruling; each article is described by the facts the ruling
% states, citing it; the office's judgments — the principal use, the essential
% character of a composite good or set, the answer to a claim that the article
% belongs to a heading outside the model — carry who made them and why. The
% ruling's code is NOT a fact: the expectation is the six-digit subheading the
% model derives from them.
% Selection: the most recent valid German BTI for 3923.21, 3923.90, 3924.90
% and 3926.90 (September 2026); the first six digits of the BTI's CN code are
% the HS subheading compared. See README.md for the method and results.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base plastics ebti includes these resources:
    plastics.

the knowledge base plastics ebti includes:

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% The bowl clamp turns on CBP's judgment of its principal use: which judgment
% would have put it in heading 3924, as the importer asked?
query household is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the heading of the self-feeding bowl clamp is 3924.

% BTI DEBTI19479/26-1, Hauptzollamt Hannover, 09/07/2026: dog waste bags.
scenario bti_debti19479_26_1 is:
    the dog waste bags is a manufactured article, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1.
    the dog waste bags is made of plastics, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1.
    the dog waste bags is shaped as sack, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1.
    the dog waste bags contains 100 percent of polyethylene, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1.
    the dog waste bags is printed with motifs, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1.
    the principal use of the dog waste bags is packing of goods,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1,
        because "bags of welded HDPE film classified as articles for the conveyance or packing of goods".
    the printing of the dog waste bags is merely subsidiary,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI19479/26-1,
        because "the BTI cites Section VII note 2 and keeps the printed bags in Chapter 39".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the dog waste bags is 3923.21"].

% BTI DEBTI22676/26-1, Hauptzollamt Hannover, 26/06/2026: foam packaging insert.
scenario bti_debti22676_26_1 is:
    the foam packaging insert is a manufactured article, as stated in BTI DEBTI22676/26-1.
    the foam packaging insert is made of plastics, as stated in BTI DEBTI22676/26-1.
    the principal use of the foam packaging insert is packing of goods,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI22676/26-1,
        because "a transport packaging for parts of dial gauges".
    the foam packaging insert is claimed to belong to sheets of heading 3921, as stated in BTI DEBTI22676/26-1.
    the claim that the foam packaging insert belongs to sheets of heading 3921 is rejected,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI22676/26-1,
        because "the block has been worked further (specific cut-outs), so it is not a good of heading 3921 (Chapter 39 note 10)".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the foam packaging insert is 3923.90"].

% BTI DEBTI41932/25-1, Hauptzollamt Hannover, 11/11/2025: drinking bottle.
scenario bti_debti41932_25_1 is:
    the drinking bottle is a manufactured article, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the drinking bottle is a composite good, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the plastic body and lid of the drinking bottle is a component of the drinking bottle, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the silicone seal of the drinking bottle is a component of the drinking bottle, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the carrying strap of the drinking bottle is a component of the drinking bottle, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the plastic body and lid of the drinking bottle is made of plastics, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1.
    the essential character of the drinking bottle is given by the plastic body and lid of the drinking bottle,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1,
        because "by their extent and their importance for the use, the plastics give the character".
    the principal use of the drinking bottle is household use,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI41932/25-1,
        because "a bottle for carrying drinks, used in the household, outdoors and when travelling; not tableware or kitchenware of subheading 3924.10".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the drinking bottle is 3924.90"].

% BTI DEBTI47170/25-1, Hauptzollamt Hannover, 14/01/2026: system tool crate.
scenario bti_debti47170_25_1 is:
    the system tool crate is a manufactured article, as stated in BTI DEBTI47170/25-1.
    the system tool crate is made of plastics, as stated in BTI DEBTI47170/25-1.
    the principal use of the system tool crate is carrying tools,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI47170/25-1,
        because "an open crate of a modular tool-case system for transporting and storing tools of all kinds; not an article for the packing of goods (Explanatory Note to heading 3923)".
    the system tool crate is claimed to belong to containers of heading 4202, as stated in BTI DEBTI47170/25-1.
    the claim that the system tool crate belongs to containers of heading 4202 is rejected,
        according to Hauptzollamt Hannover, as stated in BTI DEBTI47170/25-1,
        because "the crate is not fitted to hold particular tools, so it is neither named in heading 4202 nor similar to the goods named there".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the system tool crate is 3926.90"].
